[2m[2mSession[0m: [1;33mgoogle_gemini-3.5-flash-integration-bug-trial-1[0m[0m
I have resolved both production incidents by making the concurrent operations safe and reversing inventory reservation upon charge failure.

Specifically, I added an `asyncio.Lock` to `Inventory` to serialize stock checks and decrements, and restructured the `checkout` function in `checkout.py` to decrement/reserve inventory first, attempting the payment charge next, and refunding (incrementing) the inventory if the charge fails. All tests and concurrent simulations now pass successfully with no errors or negative inventory.
